// Analysis of the axiomata codebase itself.
// Generated by /axm — a meta knowledge base describing the project that powers it.

// ── Goals ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

goal bridge-human-agent "humans and AI agents query the same @knowledge-base with the same tools — neither needs a translation layer or a separate API"
goal decision-audit-trail "every architectural and product decision is recorded with its reasoning so future contributors do not have to reverse-engineer the why"
goal repo-native-knowledge "decision context lives in the same repository as the code that implements it, versioned together, instead of in an external wiki that drifts out of date"
goal low-friction-authoring "recording a decision is cheap enough that authors do it in the moment — auto-generated IDs, no schema design step before writing the first statement"

// ── Domain vocabulary ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

domain-term knowledge-base "a directory of .axm files governed by an optional axmconfig.json; files within a KB share a single flat namespace, and the config can import a second KB whose statements are available for reference but not redeclaration"
domain-term statement "a typed, named entry with a string value — the basic unit stored in a @knowledge-base"
domain-term type-declaration "a named category statements can belong to, declared via the type keyword"
domain-term reference "an at-prefixed id token inside a @statement value that points to another @statement"
domain-term canonical-form "the storage form: type id \"value\" — the only form written to disk by tools; type is always required"

// ── Components ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

component core "shared types and error definitions consumed by every other package — AST, KnowledgeIndex, AxmError, Range"
component parser "stateless transformation pipeline — tokenizeLine → parseLine → parseFile → buildIndex"
component cli "the axm command-line tool built on @core and @parser; commands live in cli/src/commands/; includes init, init-plan, check, index, query, search, add, refs, rename, summary"
component lsp "the axiomata-lsp language server built on @core and @parser; serves diagnostics, hover, completion, go-to-def, references, rename"
component tree-sitter-axm "tree-sitter grammar producing parser.c and queries/highlights.scm for editor syntax highlighting; sibling to the TS pipeline"
component axm-skill "skills/axm/SKILL.md — Claude Code slash command (/axm) that orients, searches, and queries a KB using the CLI; delivers @bridge-human-agent by giving agents the same query surface as humans"
component axm-plan-skill "skills/axm-plan/SKILL.md — Claude Code slash command (/axm-plan) that interviews the user to populate a plan KB; drives toward goal, task, spike, discussion, risk, unknown, decision, milestone coverage; queries the global KB and codebase before asking the user"
component load-kb "cli/src/load-kb.ts — reads axmconfig.json (include patterns, optional import), loads the imported global KB recursively as read-only context, parses local files, and passes both to @indexer; falls back to a recursive directory walk when no config is present"
component indexer "parser/src/indexer.ts — runs the two-pass index/resolution algorithm and emits DuplicateId, DuplicateType, UnknownType, UnresolvedReference errors"

// ── Principles ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

principle plain-text-first "the format is human-readable plain text and the CLI is the primary interface — every operation an LSP performs must also be reachable from the shell. This is what delivers @repo-native-knowledge: a .axm file is a normal text file, diffable in git like any other source"
principle agent-readable "every CLI command accepts --json so AI agents can use the same operations humans do — the mechanism that delivers @bridge-human-agent"
principle flat-namespace "within a single KB, all statements and types share one namespace across all files — this is what makes cross-file @reference work transparently. Between KBs, namespaces are separate: an imported KB's statements resolve but cannot be redeclared"
principle stateless-pipeline "@parser is a pure transformation chain — input text in, AST/index/errors out; no I/O, no globals. @load-kb is the only piece that touches the filesystem on the parser side"
principle errors-as-data "parse and index errors are first-class data structures (the AxmError union in @core) with codes and ranges, not strings — @cli formats them for humans and @lsp converts them to LSP diagnostics"
principle share-the-pipeline "the @lsp and @cli both consume the same @parser output; there is no separate parsing path for the language server"

// ── Architectural decisions ──────────────────────────────────────────────────

decision pnpm-workspace-with-turbo "use pnpm workspaces + Turbo for the monorepo build graph; packages depend on each other via workspace:* references"
decision four-package-split "split the system into @core (types), @parser (logic), @cli (binary), @lsp (server) — @core has no runtime code, just types, so it can be a dependency without coupling"
decision two-pass-indexing "indexing is two passes: first collect all declarations, then resolve references — this is what lets a statement forward-reference another statement in any file regardless of order"
decision tokenize-per-line "the tokenizer operates one line at a time — a statement cannot span multiple lines, which keeps the grammar trivially recoverable from any single parse error"
decision type-as-prefix "the type name is written directly as the first token of a statement (type id \"value\") rather than as stmt:type — eliminates the stmt keyword; type is required and is the only reserved word"
decision auto-generated-ids "axm add generates short hex IDs like s3f1a by default so authors do not have to invent unique names for ephemeral statements — serves @low-friction-authoring. Descriptive slugs (e.g. tenant, pg-jsonb) are reserved for things meant to be referenced by name"
decision rename-via-tokenizer "axm rename re-tokenizes each affected line and edits by Range rather than doing text find-replace — avoids accidentally rewriting an id that appears inside a string value or comment"
decision lsp-rebuild-on-change "the LSP rebuilds the entire knowledge index on every document change AND after each batch of @cross-file-watching events, rather than doing incremental updates — fine at current scale, see @incremental-indexing-needed"
decision cross-file-watching "the @lsp registers workspace/didChangeWatchedFiles for **/*.axm during onInitialized and also starts a chokidar watcher on the imported global KB root (if any), so edits made outside the editor (axm add, axm rename, git checkout, agent writes) flow into open buffers without a manual reload. URIs the editor owns (in the documents collection) are skipped to avoid racing the live-document path. Serves @bridge-human-agent by keeping editor and CLI views in sync"
decision tree-sitter-separate "syntax highlighting lives in @tree-sitter-axm, completely independent of the TS @parser — editors get fast highlighting without invoking the LSP"
decision tsconfig-project-refs "use TypeScript project references (tsc --build) so each workspace package compiles independently and Turbo can cache per-package outputs"
decision axmconfig-root "use axmconfig.json as the explicit KB root marker, with include (glob patterns selecting local files), exclude (patterns filtered out after include), and import (path to another axmconfig.json) fields — this unlocks multi-KB workflows without introducing grammar changes; absence of the file falls back to legacy recursive-walk behaviour"
decision plan-per-directory "each plan lives in its own directory with its own axmconfig.json rather than sharing a plans/ directory — isolation is structural (filesystem) rather than a config flag, so no new semantics are needed in @load-kb or the @lsp; axm init-plan scaffolds the directory with plan.axm, types.axm (task, spike, discussion, risk, milestone), and axmconfig.json with the import pre-wired"
decision global-index-as-context "buildIndex accepts an optional globalIndex parameter; imported statements resolve references and type checks but are not added to the returned local index — the @cli and @lsp each carry local and global indexes separately so listing commands show only local content while lookup commands fall back to global"

// ── Invariants ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

invariant unique-statement-ids "statement IDs are unique across the entire @knowledge-base — enforced by @indexer pass 1; violating this produces a DuplicateId error"
invariant unique-type-names "type names are unique across the entire @knowledge-base — enforced by @indexer pass 1; violating this produces a DuplicateType error"
invariant references-resolve "every @reference must point to a declared @statement — enforced by @indexer pass 2; violating this produces an UnresolvedReference error"
invariant typed-stmts-need-types "a typed statement must reference a declared type — enforced by @indexer pass 2; violating this produces an UnknownType error"
invariant id-grammar "identifiers must match /^[a-zA-Z][a-zA-Z0-9_-]*/ — enforced at every write boundary (@cli add, rename) and at parse time"
invariant disk-format-canonical "tools always write @canonical-form to disk — keeps stored files diff-friendly"
invariant type-not-reserved "the word 'type' cannot be used as a type name or statement id because it is the only keyword in the grammar"

// ── Constraints ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

constraint single-line-statements "a statement must fit on one line because @tokenize-per-line operates line-by-line; multi-line values are not supported by the grammar"
constraint no-publish-npm "tree-sitter-axm is not published to npm; consumers must clone the repo and point Helix at the local source path"
constraint node-20-1-plus "the CLI and LSP require Node 20.1+ because @load-kb, the LSP workspace scanner, and axm add/init all use fs.readdir with the recursive option, which is stable from 20.1.0 onward"
constraint pnpm-only "build assumes pnpm — uses workspace:* protocol and pnpm-workspace.yaml; npm/yarn would require config changes"

// ── Assumptions ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

assumption small-kb-scale "the @lsp rebuilding the entire index on every keystroke assumes KBs stay small — probably fine up to thousands of statements, worth measuring before that becomes a known problem"
assumption single-workspace-root "the @lsp only scans workspace folders it is given on initialize — assumes the user opens the KB directory directly; if that directory has an axmconfig.json with an import, the global KB is also loaded automatically"

// ── Open questions ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

unknown incremental-indexing-needed "at what KB size does @lsp-rebuild-on-change start to feel slow, and is per-file incremental indexing worth the added complexity before then"
unknown multi-line-values "should @single-line-statements be relaxed to allow multi-line string values, and what tokenizer changes would that require"
unknown stable-id-policy "is there a project convention for when to use slug IDs vs auto-generated hex IDs, beyond the loose guidance in the spec"
unknown publish-grammar "should @tree-sitter-axm be published so editors can install it without cloning the repo, and what is the maintenance cost"
decision lsp-config-discovery "the @lsp reads axmconfig.json from the workspace root folder on initialize rather than walking up the directory tree; if the config declares an import, a separate chokidar watcher is started for the global KB root — this satisfies @single-workspace-root without changing how editors pass folders"
unknown versioning-strategy "all packages are at 0.1.0; what is the release/versioning plan once the format stabilises and external consumers appear"
unknown lsp-missing-config-warning "should the LSP emit a warning diagnostic when no axmconfig.json is found in the workspace root, to signal that legacy mode is active and nudge users toward explicit config"
component axm-think-skill "skills/axm-think/SKILL.md — Claude Code slash command (/axm-think) that structures reasoning as typed AXM statements (observation, question, hypothesis, option, decision, assumption, risk, unknown, conclusion, next) linked with inline references; turns linear chain-of-thought into an auditable graph and delivers @bridge-human-agent by making agent reasoning inspectable and queryable"
